WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:15.807
Once upon a time,
an American moved to London.

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:19.185
And he brought with him
his pet tiger and a toothbrush.

00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:23.565
“Well, you've done it again,
haven’t y... [laughs]

00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:24.607
...haven't you?”

00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:26.443
“Bringing a tiger on a plane?

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:28.111
“What do you want to do with that?

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:29.863
Did you pay for a ticket?”

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.740
said the air hostess.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:32.824
“Yes, I did.

00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:35.577
“The tiger is very well traveled,
as a matter of fact.

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:37.537
“And the longer we have this
conversation,

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.873
the longer it's more likely
he'll do a s*** on the plane.”

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.125
How can a tiger speak?

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:43.668
Because he's very well traveled,

00:00:43.668 --> 00:00:45.128
he's educated and s***.

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:46.171
Um...

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:48.506
And at customs they’re like,

00:00:48.506 --> 00:00:50.717
“This is not something that's
supposed to happen.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.969
You can't bring Americans to London!”

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:55.972
Okay, you can't bring Americans
to London...

00:00:55.972 --> 00:00:58.850
So he brings him to a cat cafe.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.018
Because of the tiger?

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:00.894
Yeah.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.270
I should have gone first.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:05.106
But they don't stay
because they only serve tea.

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:05.982
Okay?

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.859
Okay, do something with that.

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:08.651
[Laughs]

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.652
[Laughs]

00:01:09.778 --> 00:01:12.363
He pointed at one of the
kittens and said,

00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:13.656
“This is your fault.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.575
“You're a ginger.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.910
“Why...

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.828
...are you so orange?”

00:01:18.828 --> 00:01:21.289
“Why do they only serve tea?”

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:23.166
cried the American,

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:25.752
causing a bit of a ruckus.

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:29.380
They go to the zoo next because that's
where the tiger wants to go.

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:32.217
They spot a ball, a football.

00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:34.886
All the animals playing in the dark.

00:01:34.886 --> 00:01:37.347
It's not the soccer he knows.

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:39.182
He wants to go home.

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:40.350
[Laughs]

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.976
What were the last two things?

00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:43.686
This is all you.

00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:45.146
And the American said,

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:47.148
“The big... [chuckles]

00:01:47.148 --> 00:01:50.985
“...problem with London is
there are no decent

00:01:50.985 --> 00:01:52.445
“omelet chefs,

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.322
and nobody’s talking about it.”

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:55.657
[Chuckles]

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:58.618
And then the tiger growled.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:02.455
And in the growl the
American could decipher,

00:02:02.747 --> 00:02:04.791
“Are you a chef?”

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:10.088
The tiger cuts off his leg

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:13.383
and then makes a human omelet

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:14.968
with...

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.011
...lots of chorizo,

00:02:17.011 --> 00:02:18.805
ham, and...

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:22.517
...spices from India because
the tiger is from India.

00:02:22.725 --> 00:02:26.229
Now that we're on the subject
of tigers and kitchens,

00:02:26.688 --> 00:02:29.691
incidentally, tigers are very good chefs.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.651
You know, they have good pan control.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.027
Not a lot of people know that.

00:02:33.027 --> 00:02:34.070
One sentence?

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.866
The human rose up from
the plate and said,

00:02:38.616 --> 00:02:42.412
“I will not be eaten by anybody.”

00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:45.498
He walked off into the night

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.292
and the American said,

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:49.669
“I’m going back home.”

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.713
Thank you very much, everybody.

00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:53.256
The end!

00:02:53.381 --> 00:02:54.591
The end.

00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:55.758
The end.

00:02:55.967 --> 00:02:56.801
The...

00:02:57.552 --> 00:02:58.469
...end.

00:02:58.636 --> 00:03:00.221
The end.

